<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Council of Trent</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1545">1545</a>–<a href="/years/1563">1563</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Tridentine Council</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Council of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trento">Trent</a> was the ecumenical council of the Catholic Church that met at Trent in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> in three periods between 1545 and 1563. In response to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a> it reaffirmed Catholic doctrine on scripture and tradition, justification and the seven sacraments, and ordered reforms including seminaries to train priests and the residence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> in their dioceses. Its decrees shaped <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholicism">Catholicism</a> until the twentieth century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/council-of-trent.jpg" alt="Council of Trent" width="320" height="264" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Laurom · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Concilio_Trento_Museo_Buonconsiglio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
